skill: "microcopy-pattern-library"
sections[3]:
  - "# microcopy-pattern-library\n\nBuild and maintain the interface copy pattern library: error messages, empty states, success confirmations and their placement rules, keyed for i18n and wired to the design system. Use when a surface ships without copy review, when error rates cluster on a screen, or when the design-system-engineer adds components that need standard strings.\n\nOwner: role-ux-copywriter (pod-build, design). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - search_web\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"surface inventory from the PRD or design-system-engineer; brand voice rules voice-rules.toon; i18n key registry from i18n-sync; existing library microcopy-library.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/design/microcopy-library.toon with patterns[] (surface, trigger, copy, key, placement rule); diff block for updated patterns\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Inventory the surfaces needing copy from the PRD and the design-system-engineer; a surface without a stated trigger condition is not ready for copy and goes back with the gap named.\n2. Classify each need into a pattern class: error, empty state, success, confirmation, warning; reuse an existing pattern where the trigger matches rather than writing a new variant.\n3. Draft error copy in cause-then-action form: what happened in one clause, what the user can do next in the second; never blame the user and never state a bare error code alone.\n4. Draft empty-state copy that names what will appear here and gives the one action that starts it; an empty state without an action is a dead end and fails review.\n5. Check every string against voice-rules.toon (person, tense, terminology list); terminology drift from the glossary is a defect even when it reads well.\n6. Assign i18n keys through the i18n-sync registry and mark strings that must not be concatenated at build time.\n7. Verify placement rules: where the string renders, its maximum length and its fallback when the dynamic value is missing.\n8. Write microcopy-library.toon with the diff against the previous version; hand the diff to role-design-system-engineer for component wiring and to the a11y-copy-audit for the accessibility pass.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\ndiffs to role-design-system-engineer; accessibility pass via a11y-copy-audit.\n"
